<title>ZIMBABWE: ZIMBABWE'S CHLORIDE BOOSTS YR SHR.</title>
<headline>ZIMBABWE'S CHLORIDE BOOSTS YR SHR.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended September 30</p>
<p>	    (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		  11.2 vs 4.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   6.0 vs 2.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional item	  --  vs 3.6</p>
<p>    Interest received	 2.7 vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit	 20.4 vs 10.4</p>
<p>    Shr of associates	 0.6 vs 0.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	   21.0 vs 10.6</p>
<p>    Taxation		    7.6 vs 5.9</p>
<p>    Turnover		  100.6 vs 84.2</p>
<p>Div payable: February 28</p>
<p>On register: February 4.</p>
<p>Full name: Chloride CA Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said its future without anti-dumping</p>
<p>assistance from the government was not encouraging. It said many</p>
<p>jobs at its plants in Zambia and Zimbabwe were at risk due to</p>
<p>delays by the two countries' governments to introduce new</p>
<p>tariffs to protect the local battery industries from cheaper</p>
<p>imports.</p>
<p>-- Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
</text>
